{
  "id": "u09-l02",
  "unit": "u09-past",
  "title": "You / they did",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "Past endings follow the same three levels of 'you' as the present. Just slot **-ল-** in before the ending:\n\n- আমি / আমরা: করি → **করলাম** (*korlam*)\n- তুই: করিস → **করলি** (*korli*)\n- তুমি: করো → **করলে** (*korle*)\n- আপনি / তিনি: করেন → **করলেন** (*korlen*)\n- সে / তারা: করে → **করল** (*korlo*)\n\nAs in the present, polite 'you' and polite 'he/she' share **-েন**: **আপনি কী করলেন?** 'What did you do?' / **তিনি রান্না করলেন।** 'She cooked.'\n\nThe same pattern works for every regular verb: **কিনলাম · কিনলেন · কিনল** 'I / you (polite) / he bought'.\n\n**করল** is also written **করলো**, and কিনল as **কিনলো**. Both spellings are fine when you type.\n\n**তুমি গতকাল কী করলে?** 'What did you do yesterday?' is a natural question between friends after a weekend or holiday.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "korli",
      "bn": "করলি",
      "tr": "korli",
      "en": "you did (intimate)"
    },
